# Source: OpenWRT-fanboy/OpenW1700k ubi2-oc e7a8143b1e67（fetched 2026-08-22；rebuilt diff against openwrt/mt76 59676919）
# Upstream: n/a（fanboy 自持；mt76 master b2704cf5 仍为 WARN_ON_ONCE+return，未合入）
# Reason: TXFREE 截断事件静默处理，避免良性固件事件打 WARN 并漏 cleanup

From e7a8143b1e670c9afc2405b152f46917bfef6662 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fanboy <fanboy@openwrt.org>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 15:54:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: mt7996: handle truncated txfree events silently

The MT7996 firmware occasionally emits a TX completion (TXFREE) event
whose header (MT_TXFREE0_MSDU_CNT) declares more MSDU descriptors than
are actually present in the received buffer, and which can reference a
wcid the driver has already released. It is observed once during the
initial TX burst at AP bring-up and does not recur in steady state.

The old WARN_ON_ONCE((void *)cur_info >= end) guard in
mt7996_mac_tx_free() caught the overrun, but it had two problems:

  * It emitted a full WARN splat for a benign, self-limiting firmware
    artifact. The frame was attributed to mt7996_mac_reset_sta_iter()
    because the module's local symbols are stripped from kallsyms and
    the address fell inside the span of that symbol, making it look like
    a chip-reset failure when it is actually a TXFREE parse overrun.

  * On a truncated event it returned out of the function, skipping the
    tail that frees the accumulated skbs (free_list), releases the
    completed tokens and reschedules the TX worker. Every truncated
    event therefore leaked its completed skbs.

Turn the guard into a plain bounds check that breaks out of the
descriptor loop after parsing the valid prefix and then falls through
to the normal cleanup path (skb free, sta poll, worker schedule). The
truncated remainder of the malformed event is dropped silently; MSDU
tokens that were never reported are reclaimed by the regular tx-status
timeout, so nothing is leaked and no kernel log is emitted.
---
diff --git a/mt7996/mac.c b/mt7996/mac.c
index 9f03f98..8499fb3 100644
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1317,8 +1317,8 @@ mt7996_mac_tx_free(struct mt7996_dev *dev, void *data, int len)
 		u32 msdu, info;
 		u8 i;
 
-		if (WARN_ON_ONCE((void *)cur_info >= end))
-			return;
+		if ((void *)cur_info >= end)
+			break;
 		/* 1'b1: new wcid pair.
 		 * 1'b0: msdu_id with the same 'wcid pair' as above.
 		 */
